{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the distant land of Nippon, thee doth yearn to venture,\na journey filled with wonder and discovery,\nan itinerary in the style of the Bard,\nwithout the use of commas, I shall embark.\n\nOn the morrow, depart from shores familiar,\nand set sail for the Land of the Rising Sun.\nUpon arrival, rest thy weary head,\nin the city of Tokyo, in an abode most fine.\n\nThe morrow brings exploration of the city,\nto the Imperial Palace, where the Emperor dwells,\nand to the Meiji Shrine, dedicated to the gods,\nthence to the Shibuya Crossing, the busiest in the world.\n\nOn the third day, visit the Asakusa district,\nwhere the Senso-ji, a Buddhist temple, stands,\nand the Nakamise Shopping Street, a lively marketplace,\nthence to Ueno Park, with its museums and zoo.\n\nOn the fourth day, venture to Nikko,\na city of natural beauty, and home to the Toshogu Shrine,\nthence to Lake Chuzenji, and the Kegon Falls,\nand return to Tokyo in the evening.\n\nOn the fifth day, explore the Harajuku district,\nwhere fashion and culture collide,\nthence to the Shinjuku district, with its nightlife,\nand return to thy abode for rest.\n\nOn the sixth day, visit Hakone, a town famed for its onsen,\nthence to the Owakudani Valley, with its hot springs,\nand the Lake Ashi, with its views of Mt. Fuji,\nand return to Tokyo in the evening.\n\nOn the seventh day, visit the city of Yokohama,\nwith its Chinatown and Minato Mirai,\nthence to the city of Kamakura, with its Great Buddha,\nand return to thy abode for rest.\n\nOn the eighth day, bid farewell to Japan,\nwith memories of a journey most wondrous,\nand a desire to return, to explore anew,\nuntil we meet again, I remain, thy humble servant.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.308956116437912}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.021099278703331947}, {"token": "distant", "logprob": -1.5090998411178589}, {"to